  "prefLabel": "Plc 2005.02 Notification of Pending Certification Expiration",
  "recordType": "rule-section",
  "ruleText": "Plc 2005.02 Notification of Pending Certification Expiration.\n\n(a) At least 60 days prior to the expiration of a certification, the licensing bureau shall notify the certificant in accordance with Plc 308.03.\n\n(b) A certificant who wishes to renew who does not receive notification shall contact OPLC customer support at CustomerSupport@oplc.nh.gov to obtain the needed renewal information.\n\n(c) If an application for renewal is not received by the OPLC prior to the expiration date of the certification, the certification shall be expired.\n\n(d) An individual whose certification has expired shall not self-represent as a certified CHW in New Hampshire.\n\n(e) An individual whose certification has expired but not lapsed who wishes to be reauthorized to practice as a certified CHW shall apply for recertification in accordance with Plc 2005.07.\n\nSource. #14217, INTERIM, eff 4-1-25; ss by #14388, eff 10-24-25, EXPIRES: 10-24-35",
  "source": "https://github.com/GraniteState/adm-rules-data/blob/1c92d82e0f03a582ca5b7a578588edf38de2318e/raw/2026-11-15/state_agencies/plc2000.html"
